======================================================================
KEY INSIGHTS
======================================================================
Note: conversion_rate here is conversions/clicks (per the lab's formula), separate from CPA/ROAS which are the primary cost-efficiency metrics for this dataset.
Lowest (best) CPA: Social Media ($166.89)
Highest (worst) CPA: Paid Ads ($170.16)
Highest ROAS: Social Media (2.97x)
Lowest ROAS: Email (2.93x)
CPA is right-skewed (mean 377.3 vs. median 207.5, max 15473.2) — a small number of campaigns have very high per-acquisition cost.
Sample sizes per Campaign_Type group are large (~11,000), and with n this large the t-test's reliance on the CLT for the sampling distribution of the mean holds even though the raw distribution is skewed.
